+## Line endings and the fixtures
+
+`.gitattributes` keeps text files LF on every machine and marks `benchmarks/fixtures/**` as `-text` (never converted). This matters on Windows: with Git's `autocrlf=true`, a checkout without it rewrites the fixtures' line endings, which changes their bytes and fails every digest check (25 failures in total). If your repository already contains CRLF-converted text files, run `git add --renormalize .` once after adding `.gitattributes` and commit the result.
